🚌 Bus Seat Booking
A bus has N seats available. There are X passengers who want to travel.

Each bus can accommodate exactly 40 passengers.

The company wants to arrange the minimum number of buses required to accommodate all passengers.

However, there is a condition:
- If the number of passengers is less than or equal to the available seats in one bus, only one bus is needed.
- If passengers exceed the capacity, additional buses must be arranged.
Input Format:
- First line contains an integer T, representing the number of test cases.
- Each test case contains an integer X, representing the number of passengers.

#include<stdio.h>
int main(){
    int t,x,min;
    scanf("%d", &t);
    while(t--){
        scanf("%d",&x);
        min=x/40;
        if(x%40!=0)
            min++;
        printf("\nmin buses %d", min);
        }
    return 0;
}

